[Music]  thank you  hi guys it's Quinn here if you enjoy my  videos consider hitting the like button  it's the only way the YouTube algorithm  really notices me  safe hold by David Weber is a series of  science fiction books dealing with  themes such as the use of religion to  manipulate the masses the inherent  conflict between dogma and Innovation  and progress and the corrupting effect  that power has on those who possess it  this series is set in the 24th century  at a time where humankind has colonized  multiple star systems in this era  humanity is very technologically  advanced and it seems that the universe  is Theirs to uncover  that is until they discover that a  nearby civilization has been devastated  by some other alien race  Humanity understood that this was a  hostile race of beings they knew that  this conflict would come for them  eventually so they prepared well for it  Ten Years Later the attack comes  Humanity assumed that their technology  and fighting force could fend off the  invading aliens but they were wrong  the severity of the opening a baba  attack even if it had been thrown back  had been a brutal wake-up call every  Federation world had begun arming and  fortifying when the first evidence of  the kababa's existence had appeared ten  years before Creswell after Cresswell  those preparations have been pressed at  a frenetic pace and a star system made  an awesome Fortress the surviving Fleet  elements had fallen back on the fixed  defenses standing and fighting to the  death in defense of Humanity's worlds  and they made the kababa pay a hideous  price in dead and broken Starships  had chosen to pay it  though Humanity fights bravely they  cannot stand against the unrelenting  might of the kababa diplomacy is  attempted several times but the aliens  do not respond to any human attempts at  communication all attempts are met with  cold silence the deafening Silence of  the kababa as they annihilate humanity  is chilling to contemplate a species  being destroyed without even the  slightest acknowledgment that they were  any more than pests being dealt with  with the callous Precision of a  persistent exterminator not even the  xenologist had been able to come up with  a satisfactory explanation for why the  kababa flatly refused to even consider  negotiations  they or they're translating computers at  any rate obviously comprehended Standard  English since they'd clearly used  captured data and documents and the  handful of broken scarred human  prisoners who had been recovered from  them had been interrogated with a casual  dispassionate brutality that was  horrifying so Humanity had known  communication with them was at least  possible yet they'd never responded to a  single official communication attempt  except to press their attacks harder  similar to some Concepts and other books  I've covered like blindsight by Peter  Watts these life forms are suggested not  to be conscious at all human beings are  conscious there is something that exists  within us that has become more than mere  intelligence we think and yet something  else perceives those thoughts something  else recognizes the fact that we are  thinking  books like this one and blindsight  suggest that to assume that other  intelligent beings would be the same is  a flawed line of thinking personally pay  wondered if they were actually still  capable of a reasoned response at all  some of the ships the Federation had  captured or knocked out and been able to  examine had been ancient almost beyond  belief at least one according to the  scientists who'd analyzed it had been  built at least two Millennia before its  capture yet there was no indication of  any significant technological Advance  between the time of its construction and  its final battle ships which has all  been had suggested were brand new  construction had mounted identical  weapons computers hyperdrives and sensor  suits that suggested a degree of  cultural stagnation which even pays  ancestral China at its most conservative  rejection of the outside world had never  approached  one which made even ancient Egypt seem  like a hotbed of innovation it was  impossible for pay to conceive of any  sentient beings who could go that long  without any major advances so perhaps  the gababa no longer were sentient in  the human sense of the term perhaps  everything all this was simply the  result of a set of cultural imperatives  so deeply ingrained they'd become  literally instinctual  the kababa appeared to have at one point  been sentient but over the course of  their evolution Consciousness became  unnecessary the idea that a species  could evolve to be sentient only to lose  the trait entirely is very interesting  to me it implies that Consciousness was  somehow evolutionarily useful at one  point in the species history but once  they reached a certain point in their  development it became no longer  beneficial  Humanity does eventually evade the  kababa but not before the vast majority  of humans are killed eight million  humans are sent to colonize a new world  which they called safe hold where they  would live without technology  the aliens could detect them if their  technology became too advanced the 8  million are referred to as the atoms and  Eaves the planet's safe hold was  slightly smaller than Earth and its  Planetary Cycles were somewhat different  but perfectly acceptable the safe  holding day was 26 hours and 31 minutes  long the years were approximately 301  days in length approximately 91 percent  the length of an earth year safehold had  one major Moon which rotated in a 28-day  cycle there were 10 months in each year  divided into 10 5-day weeks  the original plan had been to heavily  restrict industrialization the problem  is the administrator Langhorne has a bit  of a God complex he makes it so the  colonist's memories are altered so that  they no longer remember the past they  believe they are the first humans  Langhorne sets himself up as the prophet  of a cult known as the Church of God  awaiting  through his religion he hoped to prevent  the kababa from locating them by  reinforcing technological prohibition  with an iron fist the character Pei Shan  way understands that this will  eventually go horribly wrong on safehold  she creates Alexandria the last Refuge  of human knowledge an obvious reference  to the real world Library of Alexandria  and like the library of Alexandra it is  destroyed in the struggle between pay's  followers and langhorns eventually both  Langhorne and Pei Shan Wei are killed  this Sparks the war of the Fallen  between those who would see Humanity's  future illuminated in knowledge and  those who would shroud the future and  the past in darkness eventually the  latter wins out Langhorne becomes  deified with even the moon and special  days and times of day being named after  him while peishan way is demonized and  the ruins of Alexandra become known as  the accursed place Armageddon Reef 800  years later however  backup plan begins patronway had created  a cybernetic version of one of her best  tactical officers nimu Alban she had all  of the original humans memories and  skills at the time of nimu's Awakening  there are about 1 billion humans on  safehold  throughout the 10 books of the series  nimu Alban Works to undermine the Church  of God awaiting and promote science and  Innovation on stronghold which has by  this time formed into a Theocratic  feudal society nimu knows they must  bring down the church in order to  restore Humanity's real history and  technology so that they can prepare for  the inevitable re-encounter with the  kebaba eventually in the series we also  learn about the monks of saint zerno  who secretly protected the written  memory of the long forgotten human  Federation which at once fled the kababa  though this Series has many elements of  Science Fiction the pre-industrial  environment on safe hold is definitely  reminiscent of some fantasy series that  I've read There are Kings Emperors sword  fighting battles by ship huge Wars the  main recurring character of the series  nymu even takes the form of a man named  Merlin and acts as an advisor to King  Harold the name Merlin is an obvious  reference to the wizard advisor to King  Arthur in Arthurian Tales  the Sci-Fi elements exist mainly as a  backdrop and backstory to the main  aspect of the story which revolves  around the conflict of who chooses the  future for mankind don't go into this  series expecting everything to be  resolved quickly this is an ongoing  series with the most recent book being  published in 2019 these books are an  investment with a huge amount of  characters locations and plots so if you  like that kind of World building this  might be the series for you though I do  acknowledge that it might be a bit  overwhelming for some people  have you read the safe hold books if so  what do you think also let me know what  other science fiction books you'd like  to see me cover on this channel thanks  guys  just a heads up for those of you that  may be interested my next graphic novel  the LIE behind the star is launching  February 2023 you can sign up now to get  on the email mailing list to get  notified as soon as it launches more  information on my website link in the  description thank you guys so much  [Music]  thank you  [Music]  foreign  [Music]

